From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] SecurityPkg/SecureBootConfigDxe: Allocate the signature
 owner GUID on first use

Enrolling a KEK, db, dbx or dbt entry from a file needs
Private->SignatureGUID, which the callbacks of the KEK, DB, DBX and DBT
option forms allocated when the user opened them. "SecurityPkg/
SecureBootConfigDxe: Overhaul Secure Boot setup UI" merged those forms
into one page and dropped their question keys, so nothing allocates it
any more:

- every enrollment from a file fails with EFI_INVALID_PARAMETER, shown
  as "ERROR: Unsupported file type!"
- typing a Signature GUID runs StrToGuid () into a NULL pointer, guarded
  only by an ASSERT, so release builds write the GUID to address 0

Allocate the GUID at the start of the callback when it isn't there,
the first time it is needed and again after an enrollment frees it.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../SecureBootConfigDxe/SecureBootConfigImpl.c       | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SecurityPkg/VariableAuthenticated/SecureBootConfigDxe/SecureBootConfigImpl.c b/SecurityPkg/VariableAuthenticated/SecureBootConfigDxe/SecureBootConfigImpl.c
index 466ce40c72..34d4ea0191 100644
--- a/SecurityPkg/VariableAuthenticated/SecureBootConfigDxe/SecureBootConfigImpl.c
+++ b/SecurityPkg/VariableAuthenticated/SecureBootConfigDxe/SecureBootConfigImpl.c
@@ -4895,6 +4895,18 @@ SecureBootCallback (
 
   gSecureBootPrivateData = Private;
 
+  //
+  // The KEK, DB, DBX and DBT option forms that allocated the signature owner GUID
+  // on entry are gone, and enrolling frees it. Allocate it on first use, before
+  // the GUID question or an enroll needs it.
+  //
+  if (Private->SignatureGUID == NULL) {
+    Private->SignatureGUID = (EFI_GUID *)AllocateZeroPool (sizeof (EFI_GUID));
+    if (Private->SignatureGUID == NULL) {
+      return EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+    }
+  }
+
   //
   // Retrieve uncommitted data from Browser
   //
